{
  "__comment": [
    "Per-block resource definitions. Loaded by BlockRegistry at boot for generation",
    "and mining metadata. Keys must match terrain_blocks.json exactly.",
    "",
    "Fields:",
    "  durability      - number of dwarf hits required to mine this block (integer >= 1)",
    "  drops           - array of { item, count, chance } loot table entries",
    "  depth_bias      - optional { min_y, max_y } inclusive generation window",
    "  noise_threshold - minimum noise value (0.0-1.0) for vein/pocket placement",
    "  noise_channel   - generation noise field: ore, gem, or soil",
    "  material_tags   - flat string array used by stockpiles, crafting, and AI queries",
    "",
    "durability design notes:",
    "  - Correlates with hardness in terrain_blocks.json but is a separate concern.",
    "    hardness = minimum tool tier required; durability = hit count at that tier.",
    "  - The mining system reads durability once per block and counts down each swing.",
    "  - A block with hardness -1 (bedrock) is never loaded from this file - the mining",
    "    service rejects it before any file I/O occurs."
  ],


  "__comment_rock": [
    "Authored rock bands (rock01-11) - mined rock SOMETIMES drops Rough Stone (Alen, 2026-06-10).",
    "chance 0.05 (lowered again 2026-08-06 for testing convenience, Alen - was 0.12 earlier the",
    "same day, 0.25 from 2026-06-10, 0.50 originally). Deliberately stingy now to make manual",
    "playtesting easier (less stockpile clutter); the rough stone item's purpose is still void",
    "fill (see resources.json 'void_fill' tag) so this may need to come back up once backfill",
    "is actually playtested - revisit in the economy balance pass.",
    "All 11 bands share one profile; the drop item is band-independent."
  ],

